## Step-by-Step Procedure

### 1. Identify etcd Parameters

Inspect the static pod definition to retrieve:

- Endpoint: `--listen-client-urls` (typically `https://127.0.0.1:2379`)
- Trusted CA: `--trusted-ca-file` (`/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/ca.crt`)
- Server/Peer Cert: `--cert-file` (`/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/server.crt`)
- Private Key: `--key-file` (`/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/server.key`)
- Data Directory: `--data-dir` (`/var/lib/etcd`)

```bash
sudo grep -E "data-dir|cert-file|key-file|trusted-ca-file|listen-client-urls" /etc/kubernetes/manifests/etcd.yaml
```

### 2. Verify Endpoint Health

```bash
ETCDCTL_API=3 etcdctl \
  --endpoints=https://127.0.0.1:2379 \
  --cacert=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/ca.crt \
  --cert=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/server.crt \
  --key=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/server.key \
  endpoint health
```

### 3. Take a Snapshot Backup

```bash
sudo mkdir -p /var/lib/etcd-backup
sudo ETCDCTL_API=3 etcdctl \
  --endpoints=https://127.0.0.1:2379 \
  --cacert=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/ca.crt \
  --cert=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/server.crt \
  --key=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/server.key \
  snapshot save /var/lib/etcd-backup/etcd-snapshot.db
```

Verify snapshot status:

```bash
ETCDCTL_API=3 etcdctl --write-out=table snapshot status /var/lib/etcd-backup/etcd-snapshot.db
```

### 4. Restore the Snapshot to a New Directory

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Always restore to a **new target directory** (e.g., `/var/lib/etcd-restored`) rather than overwriting the live `/var/lib/etcd`.

```bash
sudo ETCDCTL_API=3 etcdctl snapshot restore /var/lib/etcd-backup/etcd-snapshot.db \
  --data-dir=/var/lib/etcd-restored
```

Set correct ownership on the restored directory:

```bash
sudo chown -R root:root /var/lib/etcd-restored
```

### 5. Update Static Pod Manifest HostPath

Update `/etc/kubernetes/manifests/etcd.yaml` to point the `etcd-data` hostPath volume to the new restored directory:

```yaml
  volumes:
  - hostPath:
      path: /var/lib/etcd-restored
      type: DirectoryOrCreate
    name: etcd-data
```

Once saved, the kubelet will detect the manifest modification and recreate the etcd static pod using the restored data.

Verify restoration:

```bash
kubectl get nodes
kubectl get pods -A
```

